# -trimpath and -buildvcs=false keep a test binary a function of its
# source alone. Without them a worker's slot path and the commit stamp
# are built in, so a result cached by one slot never counts for
# another and every run starts cold.
test: go test -trimpath -buildvcs=false -race -cover ./...

# goimports rather than gofmt, as in every other repo here: one command
# to remember, and it still holds if this module ever imports something
# of its own. -l lists what it would rewrite, and a non-empty list is
# the failure, since a CI job that rewrote source would have nowhere to
# put it.
lint: out=$(goimports -local "$(go list -m)" -l .); if [ -n "$out" ]; then echo "$out"; exit 1; fi; go vet ./...

# gopls at hint severity is what an editor underlines and nobody
# reading a diff sees. It exits 0 whether or not it found anything, so
# its output is the verdict: awk prints what it read, then fails if it
# read a line.
hints: git ls-files -z '*.go' | xargs -0 gopls check -severity=hint | awk '1; END { exit (NR > 0) }'

# A package that exports Code and Diff and keeps everything else
# unexported is one where an unreachable function is a leftover, not an
# API somebody outside calls. -test so a helper only a test reaches
# counts as reached. It exits 0 either way, so awk reads its output as
# the verdict, as hints does.
deadcode: deadcode -test ./... 2>&1 | awk '1; END { exit (NR > 0) }'

# What gofmt does not reach: the Markdown, which is where the rules an
# agent reads live. dprint.json says which plugin at which hash, so a
# formatter upgrade is a commit and not a Tuesday. It excludes
# testdata/, whose files are scanner input rather than prose: a
# formatter that rewrote sample.md would change what the tests scan.
fmt: dprint check

# The shell nobody compiles. scripts/tag pushes a tag to the GitHub
# mirror from a laptop, so a mistake in it is a published version
# nobody can unpublish. Named as a path because it carries no
# extension, and testdata/sample.sh is deliberately excluded: it is
# scanner input, not a script this repo runs.
shellcheck: git ls-files -z 'scripts/*' | xargs -0 shellcheck
